# Pull request build status

Opening a pull request or pushing to its branch starts the build. Check that status before treating the pull request as done.

- Read the checks on the pull request. A green local test run does not replace the remote build.
- When a check fails, read the failing log, fix the cause, push, and check the new run.
- The GitHub Actions workflow on this repo is `Build and Test (Ubuntu)`. It configures CMake, builds the TypeScript samples from the freshly built compiler, then runs the glue tests, the sample tests, and CTest.
